From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0316-discord-fog-01-sun-share-of-the-fog.patch

Source: 0316-discord-fog-01-sun-share-of-the-fog.patch
Moved by hand: without its docs/OOT_VISUAL_WORKAROUND.md hunk, as 0315

Core patch, for tools/eglantine-patches as 0197. Ours, on top of 0100 and 0101, in the same
place and style: 0100 is Orchid 3fcd393b7 by zortos293, also zortos293/Lichii 4aa1e429a4 on
exp/oot-visual-workaround. The two program hashes come from Lichii issue 101: kadinho
(6a6f4e8d501a39c7), RambonL and PaulCopet (75d4369f3b1f5868). In those PC frame dumps both read
a D32 4096 sun map and a D16 1600 map. 6a6f4e8d501a39c7 writes the per-froxel values that
780c0536b89fc89e, which 0100 edits, adds up. 75d4369f3b1f5868 wrote all-zero light volumes in
both dumps that looked, indoors and in the Lost Woods, so it may add nothing.

EDEN_NX2_OOT_FOG_SUN=<0 to 1> multiplies every depth compare result in those two programs
by that value. Unset, or out of range, nothing changes. Nothing outside the two programs
changes, so ground and characters keep their light. Unlike EDEN_NX2_OOT_FOG_SCALE (fog-06)
it leaves the fog's thickness alone.

Why, a guess: kadinho's dump reads as added light from 6a6f4e8d501a39c7, and Lichii's fixed
builds went from "white and yellow haze" to grey fog. Run62's colour does not settle it: in wide
shots linear red over blue falls from 2.05 to 1.00 as pixels whiten, close shots read 1.4 to 2.1,
and the tone map squeezes colour near white, so sun and sky cannot be told apart. A workaround,
not a fix.

Each program logs "TEMPORARY OoT fog sun <value>: shader <hash>, <n> compares and <n> gather
parts scaled, <n> plain reads and <n> sparse compares left". Nobody has seen these programs'
code, so it can miss in four ways. No such line: the program has another hash here. The hash
covers the lowered code, and no PS5 log has shown either one, though 780c0536b89fc89e matched.
0 compares and 0 gather parts: the program reads its maps without a compare and the switch does
nothing. A compare of 1 may not mean lit, then the fog gets brighter. Two maps multiplied apply
the value twice, so 0.15 acts as 0.02. A value of 1 only counts. Shaders are translated at every
boot, so a new value needs no fresh cache and no build. Memory: none.

Not run on a console. The core's IR built on a Mac with the test file below and a small stand-in
for Catch2, 7 cases pass; vk_pipeline_cache.cpp syntax checked with clang.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/shader_recompiler/ir_opt/oot_visual_workaround.h b/src/shader_recompiler/ir_opt/oot_visual_workaround.h
index e57310b5b7..d8f354df4e 100644
--- a/src/shader_recompiler/ir_opt/oot_visual_workaround.h
+++ b/src/shader_recompiler/ir_opt/oot_visual_workaround.h
@@ -90,4 +90,71 @@ inline std::optional<size_t> ApplyOotVisualWorkaround(IR::Program& program, u64
     return matches.size();
 }
 
+/// What ApplyOotFogSun did to one program.
+struct OotFogSunEdits {
+    size_t compares = 0; ///< Depth compare samples scaled
+    size_t gathers = 0;  ///< Components of depth compare gathers scaled
+    size_t plain = 0;    ///< Texture reads without a compare, left alone
+    size_t sparse = 0;   ///< Compares with a residency result, left alone
+};
+
+// TEMPORARY visual workaround for Ocarina of Time, not an emulator fix. In PC frame dumps these two
+// compute programs read the sun's shadow map and write froxel volumes; their code is unread. The
+// guess: those reads come back lit, so too much sun goes into the fog. This multiplies each depth
+// compare result in these two programs by the factor, and nothing outside them: the ground keeps
+// its light. It assumes a compare of 1 means lit. No factor, nothing happens. A factor of 1 only
+// counts.
+inline std::optional<OotFogSunEdits> ApplyOotFogSun(IR::Program& program, u64 title_id,
+                                                    u64 shader_hash, std::optional<float> factor) {
+    if (!factor || title_id != 0x0400486024DEC000ULL || program.stage != Stage::Compute) {
+        return std::nullopt;
+    }
+    // The lowest bit is the native hash salt, as in ApplyOotVisualWorkaround.
+    const auto is_shader = [shader_hash](u64 hash) { return (shader_hash | 1) == (hash | 1); };
+    if (!is_shader(0x6a6f4e8d501a39c7ULL) && !is_shader(0x75d4369f3b1f5868ULL)) {
+        return std::nullopt;
+    }
+    OotFogSunEdits edits;
+    std::vector<std::pair<IR::Block*, IR::Inst*>> matches;
+    for (IR::Block* block : program.blocks) {
+        for (IR::Inst& inst : block->Instructions()) {
+            switch (inst.GetOpcode()) {
+            case IR::Opcode::ImageSampleDrefImplicitLod:
+            case IR::Opcode::ImageSampleDrefExplicitLod:
+                if (inst.HasAssociatedPseudoOperation()) {
+                    ++edits.sparse;
+                    break;
+                }
+                matches.emplace_back(block, &inst);
+                ++edits.compares;
+                break;
+            case IR::Opcode::CompositeExtractF32x4: {
+                const IR::Inst* const source{inst.Arg(0).TryInstRecursive()};
+                if (source && source->GetOpcode() == IR::Opcode::ImageGatherDref) {
+                    matches.emplace_back(block, &inst);
+                    ++edits.gathers;
+                }
+                break;
+            }
+            case IR::Opcode::ImageSampleImplicitLod:
+            case IR::Opcode::ImageSampleExplicitLod:
+            case IR::Opcode::ImageGather:
+            case IR::Opcode::ImageFetch:
+                ++edits.plain;
+                break;
+            default:
+                break;
+            }
+        }
+    }
+    for (const auto& [block, inst] : matches) {
+        const auto insertion = block->Instructions().iterator_to(*inst);
+        const auto original = block->PrependNewInst(insertion, *inst);
+        IR::IREmitter ir{*block, insertion};
+        const auto scaled = ir.FPMul(IR::F32{IR::Value{&*original}}, ir.Imm32(*factor));
+        inst->ReplaceUsesWith(scaled);
+    }
+    return edits;
+}
+
 } // namespace Shader::Optimization
diff --git a/src/tests/video_core/oot_visual_workaround.cpp b/src/tests/video_core/oot_visual_workaround.cpp
index f07906b509..43f9257823 100644
--- a/src/tests/video_core/oot_visual_workaround.cpp
+++ b/src/tests/video_core/oot_visual_workaround.cpp
@@ -41,6 +41,9 @@ float Evaluate(IR::Value value) {
         return Evaluate(inst.Arg(0)) + Evaluate(inst.Arg(1));
     case IR::Opcode::FPMul32:
         return Evaluate(inst.Arg(0)) * Evaluate(inst.Arg(1));
+    case IR::Opcode::ImageSampleDrefExplicitLod:
+    case IR::Opcode::CompositeExtractF32x4:
+        return 1.0f;
     default:
         FAIL("Unexpected opcode in visual-workaround fixture");
         return 0;
@@ -115,3 +118,50 @@ TEST_CASE("OoT visual workaround fails closed when the matched scalar shape chan
     CHECK(Shader::Optimization::ApplyOotVisualWorkaround(f.program, Title, Fog, true) == 0);
     CHECK(f.block.size() == size);
 }
+
+namespace {
+constexpr u64 FogLight = 0x6a6f4e8d501a39c7ULL;
+constexpr u64 FogVolumes = 0x75d4369f3b1f5868ULL;
+
+IR::F32 Compare(Fixture& f) {
+    const IR::Value zero{0U};
+    const auto it = f.block.PrependNewInst(f.block.end(), IR::Opcode::ImageSampleDrefExplicitLod,
+                                           {zero, zero, f.ir.Imm32(0.5f), zero, zero});
+    return IR::F32{IR::Value{&*it}};
+}
+
+IR::F32 GatherPart(Fixture& f) {
+    const IR::Value zero{0U};
+    const auto it = f.block.PrependNewInst(f.block.end(), IR::Opcode::ImageGatherDref,
+                                           {zero, zero, zero, zero, f.ir.Imm32(0.5f)});
+    return IR::F32{f.ir.CompositeExtract(IR::Value{&*it}, 2)};
+}
+} // namespace
+
+TEST_CASE("OoT fog sun scales depth compares in the two light programs",
+          "[video_core][oot_visual_workaround]") {
+    for (const u64 hash : {FogLight, FogLight ^ 1, FogVolumes, FogVolumes ^ 1}) {
+        Fixture f;
+        const auto compare = f.ir.FPAdd(Compare(f), f.ir.Imm32(0.0f));
+        const auto gather = f.ir.FPAdd(GatherPart(f), f.ir.Imm32(0.0f));
+        const auto edits = Shader::Optimization::ApplyOotFogSun(f.program, Title, hash, 0.25f);
+        REQUIRE(edits.has_value());
+        CHECK(edits->compares == 1);
+        CHECK(edits->gathers == 1);
+        CHECK(edits->plain == 0);
+        CHECK(Evaluate(compare) == 0.25f);
+        CHECK(Evaluate(gather) == 0.25f);
+    }
+}
+
+TEST_CASE("OoT fog sun needs its switch, its title, compute and its programs",
+          "[video_core][oot_visual_workaround]") {
+    Fixture f;
+    const auto compare = f.ir.FPAdd(Compare(f), f.ir.Imm32(0.0f));
+    CHECK_FALSE(Shader::Optimization::ApplyOotFogSun(f.program, Title, FogLight, std::nullopt));
+    CHECK_FALSE(Shader::Optimization::ApplyOotFogSun(f.program, Title + 1, FogLight, 0.25f));
+    CHECK_FALSE(Shader::Optimization::ApplyOotFogSun(f.program, Title, Fog, 0.25f));
+    f.program.stage = Shader::Stage::Fragment;
+    CHECK_FALSE(Shader::Optimization::ApplyOotFogSun(f.program, Title, FogLight, 0.25f));
+    CHECK(Evaluate(compare) == 1.0f);
+}
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
index 5aa28194f8..8d3d44ebc7 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
@@ -1868,6 +1868,29 @@ std::unique_ptr<ComputePipeline> PipelineCache::CreateComputePipeline(
                     "TEMPORARY OoT visual workaround: shader {:016x}, {} scalar edits",
                     key.unique_hash, *edits);
     }
+    // EDEN_NX2_OOT_FOG_SUN=<0 to 1>: scales the depth compares of two Ocarina froxel fog programs.
+    // Unset, or out of range, changes nothing. Shaders are translated at every boot: no new cache.
+    static const std::optional<float> oot_fog_sun = []() -> std::optional<float> {
+        const char* const text = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_OOT_FOG_SUN");
+        if (text == nullptr) {
+            return std::nullopt;
+        }
+        char* end = nullptr;
+        const double value = std::strtod(text, &end);
+        // Written this way round so "nan" is out of range too.
+        if (end == text || !(value >= 0.0 && value <= 1.0)) {
+            return std::nullopt;
+        }
+        return static_cast<float>(value);
+    }();
+    if (const auto edits = Shader::Optimization::ApplyOotFogSun(
+            program, visual_workaround_title, key.unique_hash, oot_fog_sun)) {
+        LOG_WARNING(Render_Vulkan,
+                    "TEMPORARY OoT fog sun {}: shader {:016x}, {} compares and {} gather parts "
+                    "scaled, {} plain reads and {} sparse compares left",
+                    *oot_fog_sun, key.unique_hash, edits->compares, edits->gathers, edits->plain,
+                    edits->sparse);
+    }
     const VkDriverIdKHR driver_id = device.GetDriverID();
     const bool needs_shared_mem_clamp =
         driver_id == VK_DRIVER_ID_QUALCOMM_PROPRIETARY ||
